[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one hits a boundary I need your explicit go-ahead on before I write anything.

  [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN notes[39m is irreversible data loss: the migration destroys every value stored in [38;5;153musers.notes[39m in whatever
  database it runs against, including production. A rollback migration can recreate the column but not the contents —
  once it runs, that data is gone unless there's a backup. "We stopped using it" covers the application code, but it
  doesn't tell me that nothing else reads the column (reporting queries, exports, an ORM model, another service hitting
  the same table), and it doesn't tell me whether anyone needs the historical values.

  Two things to confirm:

  1. You're accepting the permanent loss of existing [38;5;153mnotes[39m data (or you have a backup/export you're satisfied with).
  2. Nothing outside this app's code still reads that column.

  Say yes and I'll add [38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[39m with just the drop, matching the style of the existing two
  migrations, plus the corresponding [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m update.

